  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5960",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 is implicated in the regulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4C through multiple indirect pathways. The drug acts as a target for several compounds, including 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid and [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which in turn target Lysine-specific demethylase 4C. These compounds are linked through a shared mechanism of action, suggesting a potential pathway where palmarumycin CP18 may influence the activity of these intermediates, thereby affecting Lysine-specific demethylase 4C. The evidence suggests that palmarumycin CP18 does not directly act on Lysine-specific demethylase 4C but rather modulates the activity of downstream targets that ultimately interact with the enzyme. This indirect relationship highlights the complexity of the drug-target interaction network and underscores the importance of considering downstream pathways in understanding the full mechanism of action.",
